            <ArticleTitle>[Prevention of the &quot;secondary exacerbation&quot; phenomenon in patients with stenocardia treated with helium-neon laser therapy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors have developed a method for the prevention of angina pectoris &quot;'secondary exacerbation' developing during He-Ne laser irradiation of the Zakharyin-Head skin sites. Intake of aevit (a multivitamin preparation) in a daily dose of 600 mg allows increasing the length of exposure to He-Ne laser in the most grave coronary cases and prolongs the remission. A rationale for He-Ne laser therapy efficacy combined with aevit is given.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
